label: Parcel Centroid
description: >-
  A point inside the parcel, area-weighted (shoelace formula). The only reason
  it exists is that the statewide Minor Civil Division layer answers
  point-in-polygon queries, not polygon ones.

  blue-ribbon's `polygonCentroid` in
  apps/etl/src/counties/shared/township-lookup.ts:20 -- a pure function that is
  currently a private helper inside the module that calls it. Promoting it to a
  node with its own contract and examples is a small, genuine improvement: it
  is verified against DuckDB's ST_Centroid "to sub-meter agreement" in a
  comment, which is the kind of claim that should be a property assertion.
fields:
  pin:
    classification: linkable
    type: utf8
    label: PIN
    description: The parcel this point is inside
    nullable: false
    validations:
      minLength: 8
      maxLength: 40
  lng:
    # This coordinate is sent to a statewide ArcGIS service once per parcel --
    # 3,265 times for one Iosco corridor run. Individually it is a public land
    # record. In aggregate it discloses exactly which parcels are being
    # assembled, to a third party, at volume.
    #
    # FRICTION (#9): no field-level label can express that. The sensitivity is
    # a property of the CARDINALITY of the traversal, not of the field. weir
    # knows the cardinality -- a spread's width is in the log -- but
    # classification cannot reach it.
    classification: location
    type: f64
    label: Longitude
    description: WGS84 longitude of the parcel's area-weighted centroid
    nullable: false
    validations:
      min: -180
      max: 180
  lat:
    classification: location
    type: f64
    label: Latitude
    description: WGS84 latitude of the parcel's area-weighted centroid
    nullable: false
    validations:
      min: -90
      max: 90
